title: Bubblewrap Network Setting Plan
status: draft
created: 2026-11-09
author: adrian
approach: "The `network` setting and its documentation already exist. This plan corrects the places where the code disagrees with the setting, and adds the proof the spec requires. Four code paths change. `join.rs` stops comparing the caller's namespaces and skips only the network namespace when `payload.toml` says `host`; it still checks all seven namespace numbers. `backend.rs` reports the `egress` field from `payload.toml` for both live and dead sandboxes, and returns the payload error when the file cannot be read. The `Forward` construction becomes fallible, so a bad port name is an error rather than a dropped port. `view.rs` keeps the host DNS and TLS mounts and gets tests for both settings. No lifecycle code, payload version, holder code or state directory is touched. Tests come in three layers: unit tests for parsing and decisions, golden argument tests per setting, and ignored real-sandbox tests for the namespace numbers and the listener. The provider spec's FR-003 is amended to match the new skip rule. The one fact the spec asserts without a probe in this repository is that entering the host's network namespace fails with EPERM. The brief reports that `nsenter --net=/proc/1/ns/net` fails; the ignored test in FR-006 is the direct check. The plan keeps the skip for both outcomes: if entering the host network namespace unexpectedly succeeds, entering it adds nothing because the sandbox already shares it, so skipping remains correct."
architecture: "The `network` value flows from the user configuration through `BubblewrapConfig::settings` into `BubblewrapBackend`. `CreateRequest` carries the project's ports. `create_sandbox` turns ports into `Forward`s when the setting is `host` and refuses them when it is `denied`. `build_view` adds the host's resolver and certificate paths only for `host`. `view.render` emits `--unshare-net` only for `denied`. `payload.toml` records `network` and the forwards. `litterbox shell` reads `payload.toml`, opens the seven namespace descriptors, calls the skip decision, enters the namespaces, forks, and compares the seven numbers before exec. `inspect` reads `payload.toml` and maps `Network::Host` to `EgressPosture::Direct` and `Network::Denied` to `EgressPosture::Denied`, for a live or dead sandbox. {{mermaid: architecture.mmd}}"
technologies[6]{name,role}:
  Rust,"The implementation language for the backend and its tests"
  libc,"Provides setns, fork, waitpid and execve for entering namespaces"
  bubblewrap,"Creates the sandbox and its namespaces"
  "systemd user scope","Keeps the sandbox alive and provides freeze, kill and limits; unchanged by this work"
  "serde and toml","Reads and writes payload.toml"
  nc,"Starts the listener inside the sandbox for the real-sandbox test; /run/current-system/sw/bin/nc on this host"
components[7]{name,purpose,details}:
  "config.rs and config_loader.rs","Parse and enforce the setting","Add explicit tests for denied, host, the default, an unknown value, an unknown key, the project-file notice and the local-override error. No merge logic changes: the existing split already ignores project backend settings and rejects local ones."
  "backend.rs: create","Build forwards and refuse ports","Replace the filter_map with a function returning Result<Vec<Forward>, Error>; a bad forwarded_port_env_var is an error. Keep Unsupported for denied with ports."
  "backend.rs: inspect","Report the recorded egress","Use data.network for both the live and absent branches; the absent branch currently hardcodes Denied. An unreadable payload remains Verdict::Editions."
  "view.rs","Render the arguments and the host mounts","Add tests that denied has --unshare-net and host does not, and that host requests /etc/resolv.conf, /etc/hosts, /etc/nsswitch.conf and /etc/ssl. The renderer already does this; the tests are the work."
  "join.rs","Skip only the host network namespace","Replace the seven-way caller comparison with a pure function of data.network. The child skips CLONE_NEWNET only for host; namespaces_match still compares all seven. A unit test checks the decision; the ignored host test checks the real numbers."
  "payload.rs","Record the posture and forwards","The v2 fields already exist. Add a round-trip test for network = host and a Forward. Do not change the version or add v1 compatibility."
  "Tests and evidence","Prove it","Add the ignored host and denied tests, run them, and write the commands, namespace numbers and listener output to evidence.md. Amend the provider spec's FR-003."
dataFlow: "A user runs create through the MCP `sandbox-create` tool. The configuration loader merges the user configuration and the project file. The project's `network` is ignored and the user's value or the default is used. The backend builds the view and the forwards, renders the bubblewrap arguments, and writes `payload.toml`. A later `litterbox shell` reads `payload.toml`, opens `/proc/<sandbox-pid>/ns/*`, and decides whether to skip the network namespace. It enters the remaining namespaces, forks, checks the seven numbers, and execs. A later inspection reads `payload.toml` and returns `egress` and `forwards`."
deployment: "Linux only, as today. No new package, daemon, socket, proxy or process. The host setting needs `/etc/resolv.conf`, `/etc/hosts`, `/etc/nsswitch.conf` and `/etc/ssl`; a missing path is skipped and the sandbox still has the host's network. The ignored real-sandbox tests need bubblewrap, unprivileged user namespaces and a cgroup scope, all of which this host has. They run with `cargo test -p agentkit-litterbox -- --ignored` and write `evidence.md`. Docker and the default denied setting are unchanged."
